      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-89347",
        "knowledge_point_id": "14527450-9b34-5982-9d87-b5a31870a70e",
        "knowledge_point": "Parametrizing Part of a Horizontal Hyperbola",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/a2f0f570ecc68de1a5b34fb3bd1b341fc83a728b026b035dde848dbf986e441b.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$",
        "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/e7ef7fd90c828767359daf69f68f406d61e3f82ad86b1f6b3a9480c99dedadf8.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "t\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
